{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the fourth generation.</b> Most of the commentators erred in the interpretation of \"generation.\" Now the ancients said: ten generations (Mishnah Avot 5:2), and it is found: to the thousandth generation (Deuteronomy 7:9), and in Job: four generations (Job 42:16). And what is correct in my eyes is that the meaning of דור is like \"dweller\" — מִדּוֹר בְּאָהֳלֵי־רֶשַׁע (Psalms 84:11) — and its measure is the span that a person dwells from his birth; there is long and there is short. And \"fourth generation\" is after his seed was a sojourner, and the meaning concerns Egypt; thus it is written: כִּי־גֵר הָיִיתָ בְּאַרְצוֹ (Deuteronomy 23:8). And so it was: Kehath was a sojourner, and Amram, and Moses, also Aaron, and their sons returned to the land of Canaan." "<b>The iniquity of the Amorite.</b> It is explained in the verse: גָּדוֹל עֲו‍ֹנִי מִנְּשׂוֹא (Genesis 4:13). And he mentioned the Amorite on account of its strength. Now Moses slew the great kings, and they were the kings of the Amorites, and five kings of the Amorites joined against Joshua, and there are other proofs. Thus said the prophet: אֲשֶׁר כְּגָבְהַה אַרְזִים גָּבְהוּ (Amos 2:9). And the commentator who [explains] \"Amorite\" as from the root אומר (\"say\") has said nothing."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:48.417299181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}